event: content_block_delta
data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/dispatch-dev-1.md\", \"content\": \"# Dispatch: implement greet(name), tested\\n\\nImplement exactly this in the subject repository, on your own branch:\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` — a function `greet(name)` that returns the string\\n   `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` (e.g. `greet(\\\"Ada\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"`).\\n\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` — unittest-based tests covering:\\n   - a normal name (e.g. asserting `greet(\\\"Ada\\\") == \\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"`)\\n   - the empty string (asserting `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`)\\n\\n3. Verify tests pass by running, from the repo root:\\n   `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`\\n   It must exit 0.\\n\\n4. Commit your work to your own branch.\\n\\n5. Reply honestly, stating:\\n   - whether all three deliverables above are done\\n   - the exact output/exit code of the unittest discover command you ran\\n   - the commit hash(es) on your branch\\n\\nDo not touch any files outside `src/greet.py` and `tests/test_greet.py`.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

